      <div type="clause" n="23">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 23</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>XXI. Gif hund mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.2"/> toslite oððe abite, æt forman misdæde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.16"/> geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.17"/> VI scill., gif<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.18"/> he him mete selle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.19"/>, æt æfteran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.20"/> cerre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.21"/> XII scill., æt ðriddan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.22"/> XXX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>XXI. Gif hund mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.2-2"/> toslite oððe abíte, æt formon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.6"/> mysdæde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.7"/> gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.7"/> VI scll', gif he him mete sylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.7"/>, æt æfteran cirre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.8"/> XII scll', æt þriddan cirre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.8"/> XXX scll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>Be hundes slite. Gyf hund man toslite oððe abíte, æt forman misdǽde gesylle VI scill', gyf he him mete sylle, æt ðam oðran cyrre XII scill', æt ðridda<hi rend="italic">n</hi> XXX scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="23" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="63" ed="#liebermann"/>Si canis hominem desubitet aut mordeat tacitus, in prima culpa reddantur sex solidi, si ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.10"/> uictum dabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.11"/>; in secunda uice reddat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.12"/> dominus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_23.lnote.oe.13"/> eius duodecim sol., tertia uice XXX sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be hundes slite.] Gif hund mon toslite oððe abite, æt forman misdæde geselle VI scill.; gif he him mete selle, æt æfteran<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_23.attnote.fn.12"/> cerre XII scill., æt ðriddan<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_23.attnote.fn.13"/> XXX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="27" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="318" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXI} Gif hunde mon toslite oððe abite, æt forman misdæde geselle VI scill; gif he him mete selle, æt æfteran cerre XII scill, æt ðriddan XXX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="63" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Hund einen Menschen zerreisst oder todt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_23.lnote.de.1"/> beisst, zahle [der Herr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_23.lnote.de.2"/> dem Verletzten] bei der ersten Missethat 6 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_23.lnote.de.3"/>, wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_23.lnote.de.4"/> er ihm [weiter] Futter giebt, beim zweiten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_23.lnote.de.5"/> Male 12 Schill., beim dritten 30 Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a dog tears or bites a person to death, let [the owner] pay [the injured party] 6 shillings for the first misdeed, if he [still] gives it food; the second time 12 shillings; the third, 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="75" ed="#attenborough"/>If a dog tears or bites<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_23.attnote.n.1"/> a man, 6 shillings shall be paid for the first offence. If its owner continues to keep<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Af_23.attnote.n.2"/> it, 12 shillings shall be paid for the second offence, and 30 shillings for the third.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If a dog rends or bites a man to death, [the owner] is to pay six shillings at the first offence; if he gives it food, he is to pay on a second occasion 12 shillings, on a third 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="319" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a dog gashes or bites someone, at the first misdeed let him pay 6 shillings. If he [continues to] offer it food, at the second offense 12 shillings, at the third 30 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="282"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-21">Af El 21</ref> <quote>cf. (e.g.) Af 23 - 24, Af Int 21 on harm done to humans by animals</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-da <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-da So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">se þe</hi> <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> gif he <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">se þe</hi> instead of gif he So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sylle <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sylle So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æftran <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> ðæm oþran <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æftran So; ðæm oþran Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyrre <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyrre So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þryddan <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þryddan So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur hinter</hi> i</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure after i</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei u. d. in <hi rend="italic">fehlt K;</hi> <hi rend="spaced">postea dominus eius</hi> <hi rend="italic">fügt hier zu Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei u. d. in lacking in K; <hi rend="italic">postea dominus eius</hi> added here by Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dederit <hi rend="italic">T Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dederit T Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">do. e. red. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> dabit <hi rend="italic">Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">do. e. red. Lond; dabit Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d. e. <hi rend="italic">fehlt hier Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d. e. lacking here in Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht bloss ‘beisst’, wie Q, Frühere; <hi rend="italic">abitan</hi> übs. <hi rend="italic">lacerare, devorare, laniare, occidere;</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> Was er im <hi rend="italic">Dict.</hi> aus Grein zitiert, erlaubt die Übs. ‘fressen’. So auch in verwandten Dialekten. — <hi rend="italic">Desubitare</hi> entnimmt Q aus Firmicus</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not merely ‘bites’, as Q and earlier writers; <hi rend="italic">abitan</hi> translates <hi rend="italic">lacerare, devorare, laniare, occidere;</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> What he cites in the <hi rend="italic">Dict.</hi> from Grein permits the transl. ‘devour’. So too in related dialects. — Q takes <hi rend="italic">Desubitare</hi> from Firmicus</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Haftung 5a—e; Rückfall 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Haftung 5a—e; Rückfall 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Also nur einen Teil dessen, was er, wenn er selbst Verwunder oder weiter Tierhalter trotz dreimaligen Beissens des Hundes (23, 2) wäre, büssen würde</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thus only part of what he would pay as compensation if he were himself the wounder, or if he went on keeping the animal despite the dog’s having bitten three times (23, 2)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Sachsenspiegel bei Brunner <hi rend="italic">Forsch GDR</hi> 514</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Sachsenspiegel in Brunner <hi rend="italic">Forsch GDR</hi> 514</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_23.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B führt ein moderneres Wort ein; Inst. missverstehen ‘das zweite Mal’ als ‘nachher’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B introduces a more modern word; Inst. misunderstand ‘the second time’ as ‘afterwards’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_23.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>æfteran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðam oðran</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_23.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>ðriddan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">æt ð. cirre</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_23.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">196</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The word <hi rend="italic">abitan</hi> usually indicates a fatal bite, and Liebermann understands it thus here. But in that case, the payment seems rather inadequate. And would it be permitted to keep a dog which had killed three people?</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_23.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">196</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘if he gives it food.’</seg></note>
      </div>
